# AI — shared rules

**Language:** every AI rule file is **English only, always**. Do not add a
Russian (or any other) rule document for a new brain. Chat with Yury stays
Russian; this folder does not. All project documents follow
`docs-english.mdc` (English only, always).

This file binds **every** brain: bird, human, future species.
A species does not invent its own laws or bypass this document.

## Living organism (cognition)

This hierarchy is **thinking**, not a physics parent. Do not derive `Bird`
from `Human` or share a ragdoll. Bodies stay on their own layers.

```
LivingOrganism
  Bird          ← first species for agent ai
  Human         ← sibling, not a child of Bird
  (later kinds)
```

Every `LivingOrganism` has **vision** and **hearing** — see **See and hear**.
The brain reads those plus faction, then writes **what** the creature wants.
Balance, takeoff, and joint pose belong to control and actuators. Torques
come only from `Muscle` / `JointFriction`. Bird lift comes only from
`BirdFlight` (the flap). There is no invisible upward force.

## What a brain may write

| Species | Brain writes | Brain does not write |
|---|---|---|
| Human | `MotionIntent` (`moveX`, `crouch`, `standLeg`, `lean`); `StepPhaseDriver.ArmWalk` / `EndWalk`; `OrganismVoice.Cry` | `AddForce` / `AddTorque`, PD, muscles, sizes |
| Bird | `BirdController.mode` (`Stand` / `Walk` / `Fly` / `Glide` / `Sit` / `Attack` / `Peck`); `SetFacing` (±1); `OrganismVoice.Cry` | lift formula, `flapFrequency`, `walkThrust`, muscles, body `localScale` |
| Any | `OrganismVoice.Cry` (`Alarm` / later `Call`) | mixer, `AudioSource` as ears, forces |
| Any new | its own intent component under this same contract | forces, another layer's gains, another species |

Do not invent `BirdIntent` without a task card.
`takeoffDelay` auto-takeoff is not the brain: set `mode`, or touch the delay
only if a card says so.

```csharp
// ❌ brain lifts the body
bodyRb.AddForce(Vector2.up * lift);

// ✅ bird: mode; BirdFlight supplies thrust
control.mode = BirdMode.Fly;

// ✅ human: wish; BalanceController holds the pose
intent.moveX = 1f;
```

## Factions

Every character belongs to a faction: human, bird, future species.
Species is not a side. An allied human and an allied bird may share one
faction. The player (index 0) is one faction; a `Flock` is another, or
several flocks are several factions.

Working names (not lore): `Player`, `Wildlife`. Lore names do not block
the layer.

Faction is **data**, not an actuator. When a card exists:

- `FactionMember` — label on the body (human and bird).
- `FactionTable` — pair of factions → `Ally` / `Neutral` / `Hostile`.
  Spawn or scenario writes the table. Every brain **reads** it.
  Do not hard-code “bird fears human” inside `BirdController`.

Do not put faction inside `BalanceController`, `BirdFlight`, or
`BirdSensors`. Do not add `AddForce` here. Do not invent `FactionMember`
or a brain without a `.cursor/tasks/` card.

The shared table is not a brain. One brain still owns one species.
No god object that writes both human and bird intent.

## Attitude

First hostility is **avoidance**, not combat. There is no hit layer.
Do not open damage, inventory, or an invisible upward force.

The brain reads own label + table + sensors, then writes only the
intent fields above.

| Relation | Meaning | Bird may ask | Human may ask |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Ally` | same side | stay / walk / fly with flock | stand / walk toward |
| `Neutral` | ignore | keep current mode | keep current intent |
| `Hostile` | avoid or stoop | see → `Cry(Alarm)` then `Fly` away; close prey still `Attack` | `moveX` away; later `Cry` |

`takeoffDelay` is still not the brain. Flock landing in
`BirdController.TickFlock` sets `Sit` (contact rest), not faction.

## See and hear

World senses for every `LivingOrganism`. They answer “what is out there”,
not “am I upright”. Tick in `Update`. No forces. Do not invent `Vision`
or `Hearing` components without a card. `SoundEvent` / `SoundBus` /
`OrganismVoice` exist (card `BIRD-6-voice`): the brain may `Cry`;
hearing reads the bus. That is not the audio mixer.

This is a **sagittal** 2D world. The bird’s nose is
`BirdController.facing` (±1): +1 looks along +X, −1 along −X.
Ahead is `facing` along X, behind is the other sign. There is no street
left/right. “Side” means ahead or behind along X, never a second
horizontal axis. The brain may call `SetFacing` (or write `facing`); it
does not scale the body or invent a yaw motor.

Do not use the player camera (`CameraFollow`) as eyes. Do not use
`Light2D` / torch as sight. Do not use the audio mixer as ears.
Do not fold these into `BirdSensors`, `VestibularSystem`,
`CenterOfMassCalculator`, or `BodyStateEstimator` (inner ear and feet).

### Vision — look

Origin: the **head** (flock: body). A cone along `facing` (±X), finite range.
A candidate in range is **seen** only if a line to it is free — occluder
is the `Ground` layer (platforms, dirt). Use NonAlloc (`Linecast` /
overlap). Not `OverlapBox` in `FixedUpdate`.

Output the brain may read (no forces): who, distance, ahead/behind,
blocked or not. Then the brain asks `FactionTable`. You do not see
behind your back. You do not see through the ground.

```csharp
// ❌ camera or light is not sight
bool seen = renderer.isVisible;

// ✅ head, cone along facing (±X), Ground blocks
// seen = inCone && !Linecast(head, other, Ground)
```

### Hearing — listen

A **sound** is a short-lived fact (`SoundEvent`): who made it, where, how
loud, what kind (`Alarm`, later Call / step / flap). `OrganismVoice.Cry`
announces the fact. That is not a force. An optional `AudioClip` is
picture for the player, not ears.

Hearing is omnidirectional. Range falls with loudness. **v1: no occlusion**
— sound goes around a 2D ledge. Direction is the sign of
`(source.x − hearer.x)`: ahead or behind.

You can **hear** a Hostile you cannot see (behind you, or behind dirt).

### What the brain does with it

| Knows | Then (first attitude) |
|---|---|
| Sees Hostile / prey close and high enough | `Attack` (stoop, no hit) — prey marker only |
| Sees threat / Hostile far | `Cry(Alarm)`, then `Fly` away (not `Attack`) |
| Hears `Alarm` / Hostile, does not see | `Fly` (alert). Do not cry unless also seen |
| Sees Ally | stay / walk / fly with |
| Grounded, no prey ahead, or just landed | `Sit` |
| Only Neutral | keep current intent |

A flock shares one cheap scan — not a Linecast per bird at 200 Hz.
Cap the seen/heard lists. Ranges are public fields, not a hard-coded fear.

## Rate and budget

Decide in `Update`, not at 200 Hz. A brain does not compute or apply forces
in `FixedUpdate`.

A full ragdoll is 1–2 heroes. A flock uses a cheap or shared brain on
`Flock` — not `Human`, not a ragdoll bird per body.

## Scenes and other layers

| Brain | Play | Stay out of |
|---|---|---|
| Bird | `Bird`; flock — `BirdFlock50`; hen — `Chicken` | `World`, `SampleScene` |
| Human | `World` | `SampleScene`; do not spawn birds |

Balance sensors are read-only. World senses: **See and hear**. No forces.
Do not mix a brain into the human `HeadlessTrial` unless a card says so.
`BirdDrive` is already silent when `HeadlessTrial.Active` — do not turn
it on for the human stand.

One brain, one species. No god object that writes both human and bird.

## Handshake with agent `bird` (accepted 30.08)

Colleague: profile `bird`, rule `bird-physics.mdc`. They write **how**
the body flies. This profile writes **what** the bird wants.

| | Agent `ai` (this file) | Agent `bird` |
|---|---|---|
| Owns | `BirdDrive` / `BirdFlockDrive` / `OrganismVoice` / `SoundBus` | `Bird`, `BirdFlight`, pose, landing |
| Writes | `mode`, `SetFacing`, `OrganismVoice.Cry` in `Update` | lift, flap, `walkThrust`, PD, perch |
| Must not write | `AddForce`, lift formula, `flapFrequency` | `BirdDrive` circumstances, Vision, faction |

`takeoffDelay` Stand→Fly is a demo timer, not the brain. Flock landing
in `TickFlock` sets `Sit` and zeroes the delay — contact rest, not
faction. After touchdown `BirdDrive` keeps `Sit` for `sitHold` so it
does not fight that write.

Card `BIRD-2-sit-attack`. Prey is the `BirdPrey` marker (position only).
Not Vision, not a hit, not HP. Do not add `FactionMember` / `Vision` /
`Hearing` without a new card. Do not edit `BirdFlight`.

v1 prey circumstances stay on `BirdDrive.kind = Prey`.

**Wander** (`kind = Wander`, card `BIRD-3-wander`): Sit → Fly → turn
`SetFacing` ±X → Glide → Sit. Seeded (`wanderSeed`). No prey marker.
Play `Bird` defaults to wander. Headless: `-birdDrive wander`.

**Chicken** (card `BIRD-7-chicken`): same `Bird` family, `BirdKind.Chicken`.
`ChickenWander` writes Sit / Walk / Peck. No Fly, Glide, or perch return.
Play `Chicken`. Headless: `-birdKind chicken -birdDrive wander`.
Threat alarm on a hen is Walk away, not Fly.

**Beak (card `BIRD-8-beak`):** every bird has a `Beak` segment. The brain
writes `Peck` or `Attack`. `BeakStrike` reads the beak collider and may
`Damageable.Hurt`. The brain does not call Hurt and does not `AddForce`.

**Flock** (card `BIRD-4-flock`): `BirdFlockDrive` — one `Update` for
the pack, per-bird seed, leash to the centroid. Not a Linecast per body.
Play `BirdFlock50`. Headless: `-birdDrive wander -birdCount 5`.

**Tree perch (handshake with `plant`, 30.08):** `PlantTree.GetPerchSlots`
(twigs first) and `SeatBirds`. The flock may `BindPerches` — that only
changes `homeX` / facing. Lift stays in `BirdFlight`. Wood is ghost:
`Bird.GhostTreeWood` ignores trunk/branch colliders. Sit is `BirdPerch`
pads only. `BirdSensors` still writes `bothGrounded` on those pads;
`NearPerch` keeps the probe alive above the flat-ground skip. Do not
add forces on the tree.

**Return (card `BIRD-5-perch-return`):** if a slot is bound and the bird
touches dirt (`!BirdSensors.treeSupport`), do not `Sit` — face the slot
and `Fly`. Do not use raw `NearPerch` for that bit: the AABB includes
soil under the stump. `treeSupport` is grounded + NearPerch + height
> 0.35 m above dirt. Glide faces `homeX` only when
`|x − homeX| > homeFaceDeadzone` (default 0.15 m); inside the slot
facing holds.
Count `perchLandCount` / `dirtRejectCount`. Body (`TickFlock`) still
Sit+Settle on first contact — overwrite dirt on the next `Update`.

Do not add `FactionMember` / `Vision` / `Hearing` without a new card.
Do not edit `BirdFlight`.

**Voice (card `BIRD-6-voice`):** every `LivingOrganism` may vocalize.
`OrganismVoice.Cry` → `SoundBus`. Threat v1 is the `BirdThreat` marker
(ahead along `facing`), same style as `BirdPrey`. Default offset 0 —
wander without a marker is unchanged (`cryCount` 0). Headless:
`-birdThreat` / `-threatRange`. Flock: one cheap see + shared bus,
not a Linecast per bird.

Body (agent `bird`, 30.08 after wander): Sit/Stand/Walk pitch goal is 0
(the 12° flare is glide-near-ground only). After `SetFacing` the pitch
spring is softer for 0.4 s — do not compensate with extra turns. This
profile accepts both; sit/fly times stay. `BirdWander.Step` enters Glide
`glideLead` seconds before `phaseEnds`. Prey faces the marker when leaving
Sit / entering Fly or Attack, not every frame. Tree perch: `BindPerches`
writes `homeX` / facing only. Glide `SetFacing` to the slot uses
`homeFaceDeadzone` 0.15 m.
